## Root Project Files

### LICENSE

The license file at the project root:

<hick:file path="LICENSE"><hick:paste select="#license-header" /></hick:file>

### README.md

The main README is dynamically generated based on which features are enabled,
so users always see accurate platform-specific instructions:

<hick:file path="README.md"># <hick:val name="project_name" />

A cross-platform application by <hick:val name="organization" />.

## Platforms

<hick:when test="swiftui">
### Apple Platforms (SwiftUI)
- iOS <hick:val name="min_ios_version" />+
- iPadOS <hick:val name="min_ios_version" />+
- macOS <hick:val name="min_macos_version" />+

```bash
cd apple
open <hick:val name="project_name" />.xcodeproj
```
</hick:when>
<hick:when test="compose">
### Android (Jetpack Compose)
- Minimum SDK: <hick:val name="min_android_sdk" />
- Target SDK: <hick:val name="target_android_sdk" />

```bash
cd android
./gradlew assembleDebug
```
</hick:when>
<hick:when test="avalonia">
### Desktop (Avalonia)
- Windows
- macOS
- Linux

```bash
cd desktop
dotnet run
```
</hick:when>
<hick:when test="spa">
### Web Application (React)

```bash
cd web
npm install
npm run dev
```
</hick:when>
<hick:when test="extension">
### Browser Extension

```bash
cd browser-extension
npm install
npm run build
# Load dist/ as unpacked extension in your browser
```
</hick:when>
<hick:when test="backend">
### Backend (Rust)

```bash
cd backend
cargo run
```
</hick:when>
<hick:when test="iroh-relay">
### Iroh Relay Server

The relay server enables NAT traversal and peer discovery for Iroh networking.

```bash
cd iroh-relay
cargo run
```

**Docker:**
```bash
cd iroh-relay
docker build -t <hick:val name="project_name" />-iroh-relay .
docker run -p 3478:3478 -p 443:443 <hick:val name="project_name" />-iroh-relay
```
</hick:when>
<hick:when test="rust-frontend-lib">
### Rust Frontend Library

The shared Rust library contains business logic compiled to multiple targets.

**Build for WebAssembly:**
```bash
cd rust-lib
./build-wasm.sh
```

**Build for Native FFI:**
```bash
cd rust-lib
./build-native.sh
```
</hick:when>

## License

MIT License - see [LICENSE](LICENSE) for details.
